+## Context on demand
+
+A loaded model holds two kinds of memory: its weights, and its context - the KV cache and the compute buffers, sized for the context window and the batch whether or not a request is running. With `--context-on-demand` the server keeps the weights loaded and lets its clients give the context back between their requests:
+
+- a request that carries `keep_context_ms` has the context freed that many milliseconds after its answer (`0`: as soon as it is answered), and the next request that needs a context creates it again. Creating it costs far less than loading the model, but it is not free: requests that follow each other carry a keep long enough to bridge the time between them, and pay one creation for the whole run instead of one each;
+- **a request that does not carry it uses the context as it always did: the context is not freed after it.** A client that does not know the option is served exactly as by a server without it, cached prompt included. The context then stays until a later request that carries a keep is answered;
+- among the requests that carry a keep, a keep can only extend the time the context is kept, never shorten another's: the context is freed when the latest of the times asked for has passed. `"keep_context_ms": 0` on one request does not take the context from another that asked for longer;
+- the context made by the load itself is not a request's: it is freed once the server is idle, and the first request creates one.
+
+`--keep-context-ms N` gives a keep to the requests that carry none, for a server whose clients cannot be changed.
+
+This is the `keep_alive` of other runners applied to the context instead of the whole model, in milliseconds because the useful values are short. It differs from [sleeping on idle](#sleeping-on-idle), which unloads the weights too and pays a full load on the next request; the two can be used together.
+
+Notes:
+
+- The memory of the context is given back to the device, so several servers sharing one device only need room for the contexts that work at the same time. If the context cannot be created because that memory is in use, the request is answered with error `503` (`unavailable_error`) and can be retried; the server stays up.
+- The cached prompt of a slot lives in the KV cache and is freed with it: a conversation whose context was freed evaluates its prompt again. Give its requests a `keep_context_ms` as long as the pause expected before the next one, or none at all.
+- `/health`, `/props`, `/models`, `/metrics`, `/slots`, tokenization and detokenization do not need the context and do not create it.
+- The context is created with the parameters of the first load: the same size, batch sizes and device placement, without fitting them again to the memory that is free at that moment.
+- Not supported yet together with speculative decoding or a multimodal projector: the server refuses to start.
+
+`GET /metrics` reports `llamacpp:context_loaded` (1 while the context exists), `llamacpp:context_creations_total` and `llamacpp:context_creation_seconds_total`.
+
 ## More examples
 
 ### Interactive mode
